  "id": "chunk_38",
  "chunk": "On the other hand, one might argue whether human-like understanding and\nreasoning is even a necessary condition toward general intelligence or whether\nsome alien-like intelligence (however hard to imagine) also suffices.\nAs the AI community continues to develop more powerful language models,\nit is important to maintain realistic assessments of their capabilities and limi-\ntations. The impressive linguistic fluency of LLMs should not be mistaken for\nhuman-like intelligence, particularly in domains requiring the kind of adaptive,\nmetacognitive problem-solving that even easy-to-play games likeZorkdemand.\nUnderstanding these limitations is essential not only for advancing AI research\nbut also for developing appropriate applications and setting realistic expecta-\ntions about the path toward artificial general intelligence. Our findings suggest\nthat current LLMs face substantial challenges in domains requiring adaptive",
